Description: Do not crash when the child of a Wayland client subprocess exits right after it started.
 meta_wayland_client_new_subprocess() reads the pid of the child with g_subprocess_get_identifier() and passes it to
 g_ascii_strtoll(). GLib's worker thread reaps the child as soon as it exits, after which the identifier is NULL, and
 g_ascii_strtoll() dereferences it. A child killed right after it started can be reaped before the main thread reads
 the identifier: at a logout, systemd sends SIGTERM to every process of GNOME Shell's unit, also to the desktop icons
 process DING has just started, and GNOME Shell crashed with SIGSEGV in a CI run of the session test lock-screen.
 .
 The pid of a client whose child is already reaped is left 0, and the client is returned with its subprocess as for
 any other child.
 .
 With a library preloaded into GNOME Shell which delays g_subprocess_get_identifier() by 50 ms, so that GLib reaps a
 child running /bin/true before mutter reads the identifier, GNOME Shell crashed at the first such start without the
 change, and with it returned 20 of 20 such clients with pid 0, their subprocesses reporting the exit status. Without
 the delay, a loop which starts /bin/true this way every millisecond and logs out crashed GNOME Shell in 2 of 29
 logouts without the change.
Author: Mitar
Bug-Ubuntu: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2126624
Last-Update: 2026-11-16
diff --git a/src/wayland/meta-wayland-client.c b/src/wayland/meta-wayland-client.c
--- a/src/wayland/meta-wayland-client.c
+++ b/src/wayland/meta-wayland-client.c
@@ -228,6 +228,7 @@ meta_wayland_client_new_subprocess (MetaContext          *context,
   int client_fd[2];
   MetaWaylandClient *client;
   g_autoptr (GSubprocess) subprocess = NULL;
+  const char *identifier;
 
   g_return_val_if_fail (META_IS_CONTEXT (context), NULL);
   g_return_val_if_fail (G_IS_SUBPROCESS_LAUNCHER (launcher), NULL);
@@ -255,8 +256,12 @@ meta_wayland_client_new_subprocess (MetaContext          *context,
   client = g_object_new (META_TYPE_WAYLAND_CLIENT, NULL);
   client->context = context;
   client->kind = META_WAYLAND_CLIENT_KIND_SUBPROCESS;
-  client->pid =
-    g_ascii_strtoll (g_subprocess_get_identifier (subprocess), NULL, 0);
+  /* GLib reaps the child in its worker thread, and a subprocess has no
+   * identifier once its child is reaped, which can already be the case
+   * for a child killed right after it started. */
+  identifier = g_subprocess_get_identifier (subprocess);
+  if (identifier)
+    client->pid = g_ascii_strtoll (identifier, NULL, 0);
   client->subprocess.subprocess = g_steal_pointer (&subprocess);
 
   wayland_client = wl_client_create (compositor->wayland_display, client_fd[0]);
